## Spectra rotate instead of shrinking

For a unitary operator, every eigenvalue has modulus one. The classical quantity $1-|\lambda_2|$ is therefore zero and cannot describe quantum relaxation. Eigenphase differences, by contrast, control oscillation and cancellation in time averages.

